WEBVTT

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.110
You get to burning!

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:10.930
Be yourself, be proud and face them head on!

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.150
You get to burning!

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.020
Boson-fermion exchange reaction has begun.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.960
Are you ready, Aestivalis?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:04.710
Ready!

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:05.980
Lowering pressure-resistant Aesti.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.240
Field expanding.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.330
Massive amounts of photons,
gravitons and P mesons are being registered.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.930
Aesti monitoring, proceeding normally.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.880
I'm about to make contact with the jump field.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.740
Activating sensors now.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.290
Sensors operational.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.360
Contact made with field. Now penetrating!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.300
All organic boson jumping trials have ended in failure.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:39.520
In the six months since the Nadesico vanished and reappeared in Lunar orbit,

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.770
reports indicated the Crocus appeared on Mars before it disappeared on Earth.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.690
Boson jumping seems to be unlike teleportation.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:49.650
In either case,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.810
the theory that CCs are the key to boson jumping seems to have been disproved.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.120
I disagree.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.190
According to the data that I collected onboard the Nadesico,

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.060
organic boson jumping is still a distinct possibility.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.120
I'll make sure that Nergal will profit from this.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.810
May I be given the chance?

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.960
There is No Single "Truth"

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.370
I'm so excited about being invited to Akatsuki-san's room!

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:20.870
What should we wear?

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.830
I never imagined Christmas on a battleship could be so special.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.590
Isn't Christmas wonderful?!

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.830
Yeah, I'm glad I got on the Nadesico.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.210
Come on, I see idle hands!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.890
You have to work hard to get stuff done,

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.040
or we won't be able to take off early tonight.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.280
Everyone, let's go out and party!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.150
Let's spend a wonderful night together!

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.940
The Lord cometh to thou...

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.230
Bearing presents.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.330
Bearing flowers.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.440
The Lord cometh carrying Champagne!

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.180
... galactic Merry Christmas

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.040
Okay!

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.820
Looks just fine!

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.280
It looks a little crooked to me.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.580
Nergal Heavy Industries sponsored Christmas party?

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.360
Yes, I thought it'd be nice if we all had a bash together now and then.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.190
You're always making others abashed.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.730
But we've already been invited to Akatsuki-san's party.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.040
So, what's the lineup for yours?

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.280
Lineup?

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.930
Who's all coming?!

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.760
It's a galactic Merry Christmas for everyone

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.540
Are you coming, Megu-chan?

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.520
I have to pass. I want to spend Christmas...

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.010
I want to spend Christmas alone with someone special. Right?

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.510
Nabeyaki Udon, please!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.410
That's it!

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.860
Well, this isn't about love or anything.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.970
Yeah, it's about friendship.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.330
Captain, I'll have to pass too!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.890
Tenkawa! Where are you, Tenkawa?!

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:53.400
ten no hikari wa subete hoshi

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.160
Curious, I wonder where Tenkawa ran off to.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.970
MERIKURIMASU wa darenimo yattekuru

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.060
No, it doesn't come to everyone.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.770
You aliens, today will be the last time.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:05.550
Do they ask how others feel?

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.860
Tenkawa! Aren't you in there, Tenkawa?

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:07.620
Do they ask how others feel?

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:07.670
Launch Space Gangar!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.580
Tenkawa! Aren't you in there, Tenkawa?

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.590
Next week, the final episode:

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.490
"The Great Battle - Gekiganger Forever"

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.400
The final episode...

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:16.750
Let's Gekiga-in.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.190
I've watched all the episodes through thirty-eight,

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.510
but I just can't get myself to watch the final episode.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.760
This is perfect! Behold, the deluxe party facility!

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.720
The Super Love Attack Game and

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.550
Seiya Special Neruton Machine!

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:32.180
Neruton?

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:35.230
Come hither, dear fair maidens!

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.790
But everyone said that they were going to Akatsuki-san's party.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:47.960
There.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.810
You're being too playful.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.810
Don't worry. No one will come.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.590
Why not someplace like this once in a while?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:56.920
Ecchi...

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.010
What's this?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.980
Are you telling me to leave the Nadesico?

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.360
It's a transfer to the main office.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.020
You're not telling me that you can't stand having me in the same workplace?

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:10.930
You're misunderstanding me.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.560
The Nadesico will become an increasingly dangerous place.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.590
It's dangerous enough already with all the eager wolves around.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.820
The crew will be drafted officially.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.100
Once that happens, you won't be able to leave easily.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:26.310
So, this is your Christmas present?

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:32.650
Go Home! Go Home! Go Home!

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.220
Yocosca Bay - UEAF Battleship Dock

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:38.910
We can't have a military vessel's crew made of civilians indefinitely.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.040
Normally, everyone would be booted off,

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.250
but I went through extraordinary steps to request

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.200
that the current crew of the Nadesico be smoothly incorporated into the military.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.890
Who asked you to do this?

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:52.700
This is very difficult for me to say, but...

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:58.310
After calculating all of UEAF's damages from Omoikane's rampage recently,

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.680
we would not only be unable to pay you,

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:04.110
but we'd have to have you pay part of the compensation to the military.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.030
Two weeks ago, a mysterious explosion erupted on a recaptured part of the Moon.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:12.280
The Nadesico might be merged into the Lunar Theater Fleet.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:13.650
There is little time left.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.070
Even if you do leave this ship, you'd be subjected to annoying surveillance.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:19.940
So please, accept this offer!

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.920
What will you do, Akito-san?

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.380
Me? I'm not inclined to make war my job, but...

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.940
Oh, you won't have to worry.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:28.630
What?

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.730
We can't leave an Aestivalis in the hands of a novice forever,

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:35.560
so we're getting another superb pilot as your replacement.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:39.480
Nice to meet you.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.830
Then, Akito will concentrate on being a cook?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.800
According to our records,

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.780
based on his recklessness on Tenician Island and the black hole gun operation,

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.710
we cannot regard you as being soldier material.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:53.540
We'd like you to help the war effort as a civilian away from the front.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.620
Of course, this will mean you will be under surveillance.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.660
So, you're telling me to leave the Nadesico?

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.540
This just wasn't meant to be your place.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.470
You've done a wonderful job, Tenkawa-san.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.510
It's unfortunate that this should happen,

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:12.260
but I'm sure we will be able to greet one another

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.920
with smiles once we have defeated the Jovian Lizards.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.600
I wish I could have enjoyed your cooking.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:30.950
I'm leaving as well!

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.700
Merry Christmas, the party tonight will be so wonderful
MERIKURIMASU konya wa omatsuri yo

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:34.910
Merry Christmas, the party tonight will be so wonderful

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:35.940
If it's only for one night, why not enjoy yourself?

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:39.700
hitoban dake nara oosawagi
If it's only for one night, why not enjoy yourself?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:39.980
If it's only for one night, why not enjoy yourself?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:40.760
I don't want to miss out on my own special deity

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:47.690
watashi dake no kamisama wo mi no gashite mo MAIPENRAI!

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.260
They told me they don't need me!

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.880
Being a soldier means you need to do anything that they order!

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:54.800
Please calm down, Akito!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.160
Let's talk this over once more.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.750
Are you just going to leave your lover behind?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:58.720
You're not my lover!

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:02.930
You just aren't.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.020
Sorry I kept you, Akito-san.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:09.610
Megumi-chan?

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.050
Yurika-san, thank you for all your care.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:14.100
Come on, let's go, Akito-san.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:16.620
Wait, we're not done!

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:22.250
They look like newlyweds!

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:26.830
Akito, baka.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.380
What are you going to do, Megumi-chan?

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.540
You first, Akito-san.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.500
I guess I'll be a cook again.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:39.650
But I wonder if they'll call me a washed-up pilot again?

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:42.870
You know, I go around saying I want to be this and that,

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.350
but in the end, no one wants me.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:46.780
That's not true!

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:47.610
Certainly not.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.570
Mind if we ask for you?

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.700
You're just saying that to keep him under your supervision!

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.910
Well? This is a job that only you can do.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.080
Only me?

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.460
You know that the Jovian Lizards use the Chulips

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:07.480
to conduct a form of instant movement, or boson jumping.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.260
So they can flood the front with an almost infinite number of units.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:14.170
Nergal is rushing to unlock the secrets of this system independently of the military.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:19.910
The Jovian Lizards only use unmanned weapons, and the crew of the Crocus were all dead.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:24.270
How was it that the Nadesico was able to successfully boson jump with no loss of life?

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:27.560
The secret to this has to do with this person, Akito-kun.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.170
Inez-san?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.980
She expressed an interest in our research.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:35.500
These people want to make organic boson jumping a reality.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.910
If we could send manned weapon to Mars and Jupiter, then the current strategic trend could be reversed.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.920
In any case, Earth doesn't have the technology

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.420
to build unmanned weapons as sophisticated as the Jovians'.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:50.890
Beyond that, even the Jovians can't use organic boson jumping.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.670
We must move beyond them before they achieve that technology!

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.650
There's no doubt you have a mysterious ability that enables you to do that.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.510
Earth needs your ability.

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.080
Why does it have to be Akito-san?!

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.070
Akito-san is just a pilot!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.880
This is a Chulip Crystal, CC for short.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.890
It was found on Mars.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.230
You've seen it before, haven't you?

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.900
It's like the one my father left me. I lost it on Mars.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.880
CCs were first discovered in the mines of the Martian polar caps.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.710
From then on, Nergal took control of the entire operation.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:34.960
This is a CC.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.080
These are all CCs.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.840
So, are you surprised?

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.890
I never thought there could be this many.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:44.790
So, what happened to your CC?

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:49.980
This crystal's formation is identical to that of the Chulip.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:54.570
My hypothesis is that CCs are the trigger for boson jumping!

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:58.490
That day, didn't you jump? From Mars to Earth?

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:00.780
From Mars

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:02.330
to Earth?

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:04.360
Jump?

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.810
When I came to, I was on Earth.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:22.540
When I came to, the stone in my pendant was gone.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.390
See?! You've got to help us out!

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:29.660
The priceless data that you and Inez-san can provide will insure a bright future for humanity.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.580
Erina Won!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:30.980
Yes?

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:31.970
A word, please.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.800
So, you've already proceeded with live experiments?

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:49.140
I'm sorry. We were so bored that we followed you here.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:51.040
It appears successful experiments are still out of reach.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.600
Well, that's...

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:59.050
I get it. You mean, you want Inez-san and me to be guinea pigs!

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.690
Guinea pigs? What's wrong with that?!

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:02.880
You're a failure, aren't you?!

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.490
For the sake of humanity?

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:07.010
You'd get more respect as a guinea pig!

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:09.560
To be that?

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.840
You can do it! t'll be a success!

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:13.940
Please cooperate!

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:14.650
Okay?

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:16.770
Are you going to stop him?

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:18.890
He'll be back.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.210
Where he is now, he's just a failure.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.030
You're all over him.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.350
What are you saying?!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:27.780
You said something about doing this

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.530
before the Jovians obtain the technology to conduct organic boson jumping, right?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:39.090
In other words, they too found the phase transition engine and Chulip someplace.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.230
Force field inoperable!

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:46.640
A powerful distortion field has arisen from inside the Chulip!

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.760
Massive amounts of boson particles are being recorded!

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:54.190
If the research probes made it to the enemy's home planet, then they'd know

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.480
that Earth has started experimenting with the idea of organic boson jumping.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.650
Then, it would be natural for them

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:02.650
to hamper and destroy any advances that the enemy made.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:04.610
Here they come.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:09.990
That can't be.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:10.990
That's...

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.470
I told this young lady to marry my friend Chris.

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.370
Marry Chris, Miss.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:25.020
Mommy, Mommy, please buy me that crimson paint.

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:28.430
You're such a foolish boy. How can I when we're deep in red ink?

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.200
You're just too much.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.140
I felt as if I was going to suffocate if I stayed at that company I quit.

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:37.300
That's why...

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.390
Are you sure?

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:43.370
Emergency

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:43.680
Merry Christmas comes to each and every one of us...

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:46.150
Jovian lizard's signal in the city.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:46.370
Damn it!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:47.650
Emergency

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.010
What is that? A Gekiganger?!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.610
Looks like the UEAF units were wiped out.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.950
The hostile units possess, however small, gravity blasts cannons.

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:29.860
Everyone, be careful!

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:32.150
...refrain from driving, and stay away from the Kawasaki district

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:37.620
as you will hamper the efforts of the UEAF to thwart the enemy.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:39.560
Furthermore, the Jovian Lizard units are being intercepted by the Aestivalis troops from the Nadesico.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:43.500
Didn't you promised to forget about Nadesico and celebrate Christmas with me?

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:44.400
But...

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:45.980
Do you want to fight?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.010
It's not about wanting to fight.

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:52.600
With Mars gone, if I lose the Nadesico,

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.300
I'll have lost the things I most want to protect.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.300
Am I not enough?

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.310
Is it not enough to protect me?

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:01.810
Please look.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.820
Everyone looks cheerful. They look detached.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.870
But they are all desperate.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:12.660
They're doing their best to protect their happiness in their own ways.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.410
It's not as if you have to be fighting a war to be special!

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:19.240
Safeguarding one girl or safeguarding the Earth,

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.490
either's a good fight, right?!

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:27.130
No field's going to stop me!

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.080
Eat this!

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:31.010
What?!

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:36.600
Ryoko!

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.760
What is this? I don't get it!

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:44.590
Stay cool.

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:46.520
I'll go in close.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.780
Teleporting won't do any good if I'm attached to you!

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:58.300
No!

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.620
If it boson jumps, that person will...

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:12.260
Newbie! Hey, newbie!

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.510
It's useless. The cockpit is gone.

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:20.140
Concentrate all your fire on the remaining one!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.150
Baka...

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:27.730
Baka!

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:31.050
All right, now!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.740
Thirty degrees to the left, in three seconds!

00:17:43.090 --> 00:17:45.290
With its patterns in jumping figured out, it can be defeated!

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:52.430
What's this?!

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:54.380
The worst possible scenario.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.300
It must've been programmed to self-destruct from the very first.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:58.760
Self-destruct?

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.850
It's about to phase transition with everything in its spatial sphere.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:06.250
I can guarantee that this city will be vaporized.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:09.070
Thank you for your assessment. But I wouldn't worry too much.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:12.870
Akito-kun?

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.320
Give me the CCs.

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:20.450
Hey, that's...

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:26.500
What the hell is he doing?!

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:27.600
Captain!

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:33.130
Something I can do.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.190
Something only I can do!

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:36.590
Is there really such a thing?

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.490
Can I be something?!

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:09.140
Akito? Akito!

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:13.260
Akito!

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:20.690
Well, I guess he turned into a real warrior at the very end.

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:22.860
Akito-san is not simple minded enough to do something like that!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:26.150
This isn't right! This is all wrong.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:27.770
It's wrong!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.090
You! It's your fault that Akito-san has...

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:39.360
Don't get so excited. Tenkawa-kun is right over there, see?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.170
Hey, Nadesico!

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:42.000
Nadesico!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:46.870
Oh, there you are finally! What's been going on?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.670
It's been two weeks. I've been sending messages the whole time!

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.660
He jumped to the Moon of two weeks ago.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:58.730
Akito...

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:01.050
Yurika, are you crying?

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:03.740
A ghost?

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:04.670
No, I'm not.

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:07.920
But how? Are you real? Where are you?

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:10.670
I haven't quite figured it out, but I'm on the Moon.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:11.910
All right, I'll head right over!

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:14.270
Silly, you can't just take off without permission.

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:16.940
But that's not important.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:18.190
Merry Christmas!

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:22.500
Akito loves me so much!

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:28.040
Hey, who's singing the Gekiganger theme?

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.380
Not us. It's coming from inside.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.930
That's impossible! This is an unmanned weapon!

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:41.060
Give me a break.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:48.910
Hello, everyone. I'm Tenkuu Ken, the pilot of the Gekigan Jet.

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:53.180
Dark String Universe Prince Akara sent a loathsome mecha monster.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:55.570
The only way we'll be able to defeat it is with Gekigan Flare!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.190
So in the next special episode of Gekiganger 3, be sure to...

00:21:59.190 --> 00:21:59.630
That's not right!

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:01.310
Next week, this program will be:

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:02.900
"Sail Forth! The Glamorous Captain Misumaru Yuri..."

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.430
No, it isn't! It's the next episode of Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:07.610
"Let's Go With Hot Blooded Anime"

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:08.550
Let's watch it, ...

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:10.250
Let's Gekiga-in!

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:10.940
What?
